Source: kidux-archive-keyring
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Antonio Morales García <info@kidux.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: kidux-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: GnuPG key for the Kidux archive
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. Its packages are
 distributed through an apt archive of its own, signed with the key this package
 installs into /usr/share/keyrings.
 .
 The key on its own changes nothing. It is what lets apt tell a real Kidux
 package from anything else claiming to be one. Install kidux-apt-source
 alongside it to actually use the archive.

Package: kidux-apt-source
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ca-certificates,
         kidux-archive-keyring,
Description: apt source for the Kidux archive
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer, distributed through
 an apt archive of its own.
 .
 This package points apt at that archive and tells it to accept only packages
 signed with the Kidux key, which kidux-archive-keyring installs. Together they
 are the one thing that has to be installed by hand: nothing else in Kidux can
 be verified until they are present.
 .
 It ships a separate package from the key because a package that adds an apt
 source has to say so in its name.
